tools/tool-templates/colloquium/phase1_codex.md.err:7969:9. **Medium for Phase 2. Unknown root-level configuration keys are silently ignored.** Server-entry keys are validated exhaustively ([mcp_config.py:59](/Users/jonathan/svnCheckouts/js-db-ad-astra/tools/xcode-mcp-front/mcp_config.py:59)), but `load()` extracts only `mcpServers` and never validates the enclosing object’s other keys ([mcp_config.py:107](/Users/jonathan/svnCheckouts/js-db-ad-astra/tools/xcode-mcp-front/mcp_config.py:107)). I infer this scenario: a valid `mcpServers` object sits beside misspelled root stanza `"blocks"` or `"toolMaps"`; validation succeeds and the limiting policy never applies. Define and test the allowed root schema before adding the sieve and map, so misspelled policy stanzas fail visibly.
